// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// COGNADOS — "free words": sophisticated vocabulary that rides in almost
// for free because of shared Latin/Greek roots with English. Grouped by
// suffix pattern where one exists (reliable, productive rules) and by
// shared-root recognition where it doesn't (the high-register literary
// vein — this is where words like "escrúpulos" and "sombrío" live).
// FALSOS = look-alikes that are traps, not gifts. Kept as its own family
// so it's clearly flagged rather than mixed in with the reliable ones.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

